node_modules/
.shopify/
.env
.DS_Store
*.log

# Claude Code's own scaffolding: the agent worktrees it creates while working are checkouts of
# THIS repository living inside it. Committing them would put a second copy of the tree into
# the branch; they are removed when the work that made them is done.
.claude/*

# ...except the project's own vendored skills, which are SOURCE, not scaffolding.
#
# These are pinned copies of upstream design skills (see .claude/skills/README.md for the
# repositories and commits). They live in the repository deliberately: this project is built in
# throwaway containers, and an account-level or machine-level skill install does not survive one.
# A skill the build cannot see is a skill the build does not have, and the whole point of
# vendoring is that checking the repository out is enough.
# (The rule above must be `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`: git cannot re-include anything
# beneath a directory it has excluded outright, so the negation would silently do nothing.)
!.claude/skills/
